# CODEOWNERS
#
# Requests a review automatically when a PR touches a given path. Every
# workspace maps to the repo maintainer today; split these out to
# dedicated owners as the team grows.
#
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# REQUIRED-REVIEW PATHS
# ---------------------
# The two paths below require explicit maintainer approval before merge.
# Both are flagged because mistakes are expensive and hard to reverse:
#
#   contracts/**               — Soroban/Rust smart contracts: a bad deploy
#                                script can lock or lose on-chain funds.
#   apps/backend/src/db/migrations/**
#                              — SQL migrations: a bad migration can corrupt
#                                production data or cause numbering collisions
#                                that break the migration runner for everyone.
#
# To enforce required review in GitHub, go to:
#   Settings → Branches → Branch protection rules → main
#   ✓ Require a pull request before merging
#   ✓ Require review from Code Owners
# That rule, combined with the entries below, blocks merge until
# @frienzy514-png approves any PR touching these paths.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                                               @frienzy514-png

# Frontend (Next.js app)
/apps/frontend/                                 @frienzy514-png

# Backend (Express API)
/apps/backend/                                  @frienzy514-png

# Database migrations — required maintainer review (see note above)
/apps/backend/src/db/migrations/                @frienzy514-png

# Stellar/Soroban contracts (Rust) — required maintainer review (see note above)
/contracts/                                     @frienzy514-png
